      "message": "Hi Justin,\n\nPTAL\n\nThank you for pointing out the typo.\n\nThe METADATA needs to reflect the most restrictive license in the project per http://go/thirdpartylicenses\n\nMore important than the METADATA will be the build files (makefiles, Soong blueprints, eventually Bazel BUILD files). I am in the middle of an effort to add license{} and license_kind{} modules to Soong mirroring the license() and license_kind() rules in Bazel.\n\nI think the correct solution for large prebuilts will be to capture a snapshot of the licenses and license texts per the dependencies at the time of build and to include those under the prebuilt directory.\n\nI suspect that the license information the large-scale-change will generate for prebuilts may be incomplete, but after the license information appears in the build system, the prebuild scripts will be able to deduce them from the build.\n\nThanks,\nBob\n",
